<title>UK: Italy sets $1.5 billion five-year Eurobond, +24 bp.</title>
<headline>Italy sets $1.5 billion five-year Eurobond, +24 bp.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Morgan Stanley &amp; Co International and SBC Warburg.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ITALY</p>
<p> AMT	  $1.5 BLN  COUPON     **	  MATURITY    18.SEP.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    18.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+24 BP</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.50 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 31.AUG.01</p>
<p> NOTES    **TO BE PRICED LATER</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA	  DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ITALY     HOME CTRY  ITALY     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.5 PCT AUGUST 2001 U.S TREASURY</p>
<p>NOTES	NOT TO BE INCREASED.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
